          "message": {
            "text": "Overly Permissive Storage RLS Policies on `atendimento` Bucket Allow Cross-Tenant Clinical Document Access\n\nThe `atendimento` Supabase Storage bucket, which stores private patient clinical attachments (intake forms, documents), is protected by RLS policies that grant **any authenticated user** unrestricted read and write access to every file in the bucket, with no path-based tenant scoping. A plantonista authenticated to Hospital A can freely download clinical documents belonging to Hospital B, or upload arbitrary files into any tenant's path."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "supabase/migrations/20260815000012_fase2_bucket_atendimento.sql"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 11,
                  "endLine": 19
                }
              },
              "message": {
                "text": "Replace flat-bucket policies with path-scoped, tenant-aware policies"
              }
            },
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "/storage/v1/object/atendimento/",
                  "kind": "endpoint"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "fixes": [
            {
              "artifactChanges": [
                {
                  "artifactLocation": {
                    "uri": "supabase/migrations/20260815000012_fase2_bucket_atendimento.sql"
                  },
                  "replacements": [
                    {
                      "deletedRegion": {
                        "startLine": 11,
                        "endLine": 19
                      },
                      "insertedContent": {
                        "text": "DROP POLICY IF EXISTS \"atendimento_upload\" ON storage.objects;\nCREATE POLICY \"atendimento_upload\" ON storage.objects\n  FOR INSERT TO authenticated\n  WITH CHECK (\n    bucket_id = 'atendimento'\n    AND (\n      private.eh_super_admin()\n      OR (\n        -- First path segment must be a unidade_id the caller has access to\n        (regexp_match(name, '^([^/]+)/'))[1]::uuid\n          IN (SELECT private.unidades_gestor_plantonista())\n      )\n    )\n  );\n\nDROP POLICY IF EXISTS \"atendimento_read\" ON storage.objects;\nCREATE POLICY \"atendimento_read\" ON storage.objects\n  FOR SELECT TO authenticated\n  USING (\n    bucket_id = 'atendimento'\n    AND (\n      private.eh_super_admin()\n      OR private.papel_na_unidade(\n           (regexp_match(name, '^([^/]+)/'))[1]::uuid\n         ) IN ('gestor', 'plantonista')\n      OR (regexp_match(name, '^([^/]+)/'))[1]::uuid\n           IN (SELECT private.unidades_gestor_plantonista())\n    )\n  );"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "description": {
                "text": "Replace both flat-bucket policies with path-scoped policies that extract the `unidade_id` from the object name (e.g., first path segment) and verify it against the caller's active vinculos using `private.unidades_gestor_plantonista()` or the escala-aware helpers. Follow the pattern already established for the `banners` bucket. Additionally, enforce a canonical path convention such as `{unidade_id}/{paciente_id}/{filename}` and reject uploads that do not match the caller's allowed units.",
                "markdown": "Replace both flat-bucket policies with path-scoped policies that extract the `unidade_id` from the object name (e.g., first path segment) and verify it against the caller's active vinculos using `private.unidades_gestor_plantonista()` or the escala-aware helpers. Follow the pattern already established for the `banners` bucket. Additionally, enforce a canonical path convention such as `{unidade_id}/{paciente_id}/{filename}` and reject uploads that do not match the caller's allowed units."
              }
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "8f149eb56b1d23a4f9b3ed3f08a42fc190ffc21f243c626cad8d8a5abc9b10be"
